Here's a MATLAB code that reads an Excel file with 3 columns and handles empty cells:

```matlab
%% Read Excel File with 3 Columns
% Handles empty cells and assigns data to ColA, ColB, ColC

clc;
clear;
close all;

%% --- Configuration ---
filename = 'your_file.xlsx';   % <-- Change to your Excel file name
sheet    = 1;                  % Sheet number or name (e.g., 'Sheet1')

%% --- Read Excel File ---
try
    % Read the Excel file as a table (handles mixed/empty cells well)
    opts = detectImportOptions(filename, 'Sheet', sheet);
    opts.MissingRule = 'fill';       % Fill missing values

    rawData = readcell(filename, 'Sheet', sheet);   % Read as cell array
    fprintf('File "%s" read successfully.\n', filename);
catch ME
    error('Error reading file: %s\n%s', filename, ME.message);
end

%% --- Check that file has at least 3 columns ---
[numRows, numCols] = size(rawData);

if numCols < 3
    error('The Excel file must have at least 3 columns. Found: %d', numCols);
end

fprintf('Data size: %d rows x %d columns\n', numRows, numCols);

%% --- Extract Each Column ---
ColA_raw = rawData(:, 1);
ColB_raw = rawData(:, 2);
ColC_raw = rawData(:, 3);

%% --- Clean Columns: Replace empty/missing cells with NaN (numeric) ---
%    or empty string '' (text), depending on content

ColA = cleanColumn(ColA_raw);
ColB = cleanColumn(ColB_raw);
ColC = cleanColumn(ColC_raw);

%% --- Display Results ---
fprintf('\n--- ColA ---\n');
disp(ColA);

fprintf('\n--- ColB ---\n');
disp(ColB);

fprintf('\n--- ColC ---\n');
disp(ColC);

%% =========================================================
%  LOCAL FUNCTION: Clean a column cell array
%  - Replaces missing/empty cells with NaN (if numeric)
%    or '' (if text)
% ==========================================================
function cleanCol = cleanColumn(rawCol)
    % Replace {missing}, [], NaN placeholders from readcell
    cleanCol = cellfun(@(x) replaceMissing(x), rawCol, ...
                       'UniformOutput', false);

    % --- Try to convert to numeric array ---
    numericVals = cellfun(@(x) isnumeric(x) && isscalar(x), cleanCol);

    if all(numericVals)
        % All values are numeric → return as numeric array
        cleanCol = cell2mat(cleanCol);
    else
        % Mixed or text column → keep as cell array
        % (numeric NaN values stay as NaN, text stays as string)
        cleanCol = cleanCol;
    end
end

%% =========================================================
%  LOCAL FUNCTION: Replace missing/empty values
% ==========================================================
function val = replaceMissing(x)
    if iscell(x)
        % Nested cell → return NaN
        val = NaN;
    elseif isempty(x)
        val = NaN;
    elseif ismissing(x)
        val = NaN;
    elseif ischar(x) && strtrim(x) == ""
        val = '';
    else
        val = x;
    end
end
```

---

## 📋 Key Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| `readcell()` | Best for mixed/empty Excel data |
| `detectImportOptions()` | Detects data types automatically |
| `cleanColumn()` | Handles empty/missing cells per column |
| Auto-conversion | Returns **numeric array** if all values are numbers, else **cell array** |
| Error handling | `try/catch` for file reading errors |

---

## 📝 How to Use

1. Replace `'your_file.xlsx'` with your actual file name
2. Set `sheet` to the correct sheet number or name
3. Run the script
4. `ColA`, `ColB`, `ColC` will contain the data

---

## 💡 Notes
- **Empty cells** become `NaN` for numeric columns
- **Mixed columns** (text + numbers) remain as **cell arrays**
- Works with `.xlsx`, `.xls`, and `.csv` files

